A||||42||My7Fieros||So whats your fav fast food ?||||7||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||12-11-2001||02:09 PM||||McDonalds? Burger King? Wendys? Sonic? Krystal?(White Castle for my Northern counterparts). Subway? Blimpies? Rallys?(Also known as "Checkers" in some parts of the country). The list could go on and on, due to the diff areas of the country. "Jack in the box" and "In and out burger" are big on the west coast, but Ive never ever stepped foot in one, so I couldnt tell ya.<P>My fav? If I could eat it constantly....PORTILLOS (in Chicago). We dont have a Portillos in Memphis, but I ate it (alot!) while in Chicago, and I get it FedEx'd here....YUM YUM! Orief, Haze, Archie, and some other Chicago guys can vouch. MMMM MMMM!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> As far as local goes though, Sonic is my fav.<P>So, whats your choice of fast food?||||reg||7
Z||000001||onfire||12-11-2001||02:20 PM||||It used to be Zip's (spokane). But they don't have one out here. So I think I am gonna have to go with Wendy's.<P>Although there is this cool restaurant, downtown Seattle. 1st and Holgate. Called Donna's. Straight up $5 for a burger fries and a large chocolate shake. They even have these cool little juke box's on every table. Anyone in the Seattle area should go there at least once.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||12-11-2001||02:20 PM||||I used to have a great In&Out Burger T-shirt collection from when I was out west, but they got thrown out when they got kinda ratty looking.  <BR>I'm a big Taco Hell fan.  I know they're nothing fancy, but they're consistantly OK, and it's probably not as heart-attack inducing as McD's, BK, etc.  Also, it's the closest fast food to my house.  How's that for lazy!?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-11-2001||02:25 PM||||Checkers burgers rock!!! but since we haven't got those here.. I'll go with Burger King whoppers..<P>it's not fast food though, but one of my favorite foods from a restaurant is the Club Wrap from Swiss Chalet... I could eat those things for a month and not get tired of them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||deceler8||12-11-2001||02:30 PM||||Sonic...great food and a great classic car hang out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||12-11-2001||03:16 PM||||Subway and Swensons!||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||12-11-2001||03:31 PM||||I love Wendy's Chili and Baked potatos. I also really like Arby's shaved roast beef sandwiches as well.||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||12-11-2001||03:44 PM||||Probably Taco Smell.<P>My pancreas has finally "cried uncle" to burgers.||||reg||1
Z||000008||wkayl||12-11-2001||03:53 PM||||This may sound wierd but after our 7 day Alaskan curise I had a BK Whopper at the airport.  It was great.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">    <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haagster||12-11-2001||04:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by deceler8:<BR><B>Sonic...great food and a great classic car hang out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Haven't seen a Sonic since I left Fort Polk (had one just off post).  Greaat...  I mean Good...  I mean Alright...  I mean So So...  I mean OK food.  Chili Dogs Rule!!!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_8.jpg">   <BR>87GT Auto||||reg||6
Z||000010||fogglethorpe||12-11-2001||04:13 PM||||When "McLobster" and "McMerlot" become available, I will have a favorite. Until then, it's all just slop.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierospeeder||12-11-2001||04:23 PM||||wendys<BR>subway.<BR>pizza hut<BR>KFC<P>in that order<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||thomas_l||12-11-2001||04:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>"Jack in the box" and "In and out burger" are big on the west coast</B><P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I remember seeing Jack in the Crack commercials in Nashville last year - maybe they will propogate to your corner of TN. In & Out is excellent - we got stuck at the inlaws over 9/11 in So Cal and that was not a bad place to be stranded a week  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Whataburger on the west coast is good too.<P>The other 99% of the time at home, Wendys or Pizza Hut are good. Baja Fresh opened at the mall and they have excellent giant burritos but the mall sucks this time of year.||||reg||1
Z||000013||ray b||12-11-2001||04:58 PM||||Jewish deli passtromie on rye or a Rubin<BR>outback S H for a real burger<BR>but my kids are burgerkings fans.||||reg||6
Z||000014||WampusCat||12-11-2001||05:47 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by thomas_l:<BR>Whataburger on the west coast is good too.<BR>[QUOTE]<P>I didn't know Whataburger had made it out to the west coast.  They started in Corpus Christi, TX.  The one across the street from the HQ there is really nice.  We used to always hit Whataburger drive thru after partying when I lived in Pensacola, FL because they were open really late and they took credit cards in the drive-thru for people who had blown all their cash in the bars!  There was a WB near where I grew up in Alabama, too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||DRH||12-11-2001||06:08 PM||||Milo's hamburgers (Alabama, mostly around Birmingham)... They use their own special barbeque sauce (grilled onions on request), special seasoning on fries and the BEST sweet tea.<P>Culver's hamburgers are the best in this area(Almost any town in Wisconsin, starting to spread into other states).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||frontal lobe||12-11-2001||07:05 PM||||Oh yeah, duh.  Culver's.  I have about 3 of them within a 5 mile radius.<P>How many fast food places can you get fried cheese curds??<P>DRH, man, I don't know how you guys (southerners) can drink sweet tea.  It's like tea kool-aid!  Whenever I travel in the south and ask for tea, I have to remember to ask for the non-sweetened tea.||||reg||1
Z||000017||AusFiero||12-11-2001||07:22 PM||||In order and why:<BR>Subway (Can't get enough 12" meat ball subs, yum.)<BR>Pizza Haven (Aussie company, great pizzas, no eat in restaurants.)<BR>Pizza Hut (Only because of all you can eat and I can pig out.)<BR>Burger King (Because it doesn't look or taste as plastic as McDonalds. The toys for the kids tend to suck though.)<BR>KFC (Even though the chickens look seagull size. Maybe should be KFS.)<BR>Mc Donalds (Or Maccas as we call it. Has better toys for the kids.)<BR>Taco Bell (It's the only place we can buy Tacos takeaway. Usually part of a KFC restaurant.)<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000018||hugh||12-11-2001||07:27 PM||||Kentucky fried Chicken french fries,Checkers french fries.The only problem with Checkers fries is they are so oily,you can buy a couple orders of fries,squeeze the oil out of them and change the oil in your car.My all time favorite is white pizza with garlic(keeps werewolves away),broccoli(keeps everybody away),and fresh tomatoes(are you reading this Dan Quayle?) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000019||stimpy||12-11-2001||07:38 PM||||Oh Lord, how I miss Round Table Pizza and Togo's sandwiches from California! Also, nothing quite compares with carne asada tacos bought of a truck. Bonus points if you have to order in Spanish.<P>In Oklahoma, Sonic is of course an institution, but I'd trade all of em for an In-n-Out. Del Ranco is pretty darn good, and Charcoal Broiler makes some really fine burgers.||||reg||1
Z||000020||85ZainoGT||12-11-2001||07:40 PM||||I would have to say CULVERS&gt;.. AWESOME FOOD!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 GT all the options :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpicNEW3bsmall2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||ejayerik||12-11-2001||07:42 PM||||With the job that I have, I am in my patrol unit and out on the road 11 hours a day. I eat alot of fast food. My favorite would have to be In&Out. I worked at one in Oceanside Ca. for 3 years. Other than that, Subway is good. But the hours I work, there isn't much open exept Jack in the Box. I eat alot of that.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Heretic||12-11-2001||07:52 PM||||Booger King is great! The whoppers and poutines are excellent...I gotta go now....outside....to........Burg..BYE!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hereticsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||avengador1||12-11-2001||08:35 PM||||My favorite burgers are White Castles but I can only get them in the frozen section of the supermarket. When I visit my sister in New York I can get them fresh. I like to order 8-12 depending on how humgry I get. Their frys a pretty good also, just watch out for the wooden fork. I thought that fry was extra crunchy. That was from my drinking days. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||rockcrawl||12-11-2001||08:40 PM||||Hasn't anybody heard of Arby's?? Or Long John Silver??||||reg||1
Z||000025||fropuff||12-11-2001||08:46 PM||||My #1 is the KFC popcorn chicken.<BR>#2 is Wendy's spicy chicken with mozzarella.<BR>McDonalds is on the bottom.  I don't like anything about them.  The buns have no seeds, the fries have no salt and are cold and greasy, and the Coke is watered down.||||reg||1
Z||000026||broys||12-11-2001||09:03 PM||||Anyone like Jersey Mikes? Best subs ever. I'd rather drive 60 miles out of my way (I have) to get their subs when I could have driven 8 miles to subway. Yep, they're THAT good. They cost a lot more than subway but they taste a lot better too.||||reg||1
Z||000027||DRH||12-11-2001||09:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B><BR>DRH, man, I don't know how you guys (southerners) can drink sweet tea.  It's like tea kool-aid!  Whenever I travel in the south and ask for tea, I have to remember to ask for the non-sweetened tea.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL... You probably get the same look I got when we first moved up here if I asked if they had sweet tea... They usually point to the sugar packets.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Just not the same at all!!<P>I guess it's something you grow up with. Before we moved here, I couldn't figure out how people could drink beer with a sweet desert. I have acquired that taste now though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000028||Jaygee79||12-11-2001||11:32 PM||||I like Wendy's, Burger King, Taco Bell, McDonald's, Subway (yummy), Domino's...not necessarily in that order.||||reg||1
Z||000029||FieroMaster88||12-11-2001||11:53 PM||||Subway and Taco Bell!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000030||Nashco||12-12-2001||12:22 AM||||I have been around, and I have to say my favorite nationwide is JACK IN THE BOX.  Sourdough Jack, fries, and the biggest frickin' oreo shake they'll sell me!  Damn I miss Jack in the Box, I wish they'd spread to this side of the country.  I saw them in Texas, damn that's getting close <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I don't understand the sweet tea thing AT ALL!  I had my first Milo's tea the other day, because I'd heard all the rave reviews.  Even the BEST sweet tea wasn't that good, IMO.  It's like frickin' water down here!  If you go to a restaurant they normally give you water to start off with; well, here, some of them just serve up sweet tea unless you say otherwise.<P>A couple Seattle area specialties are Taco Del Mar and Dick's.  I've never seen them anywhere else; Taco Del Mar is especially good.  I've never heard of that Donna's place, I'll have to look into that.<P>A good one I've only seen here and there is Fazoli's...fast Italian food!  It's VERY good, little pricey for fast food, but they call it good food fast, and it is!<P>In general, when I'm slummin' or travelling, I like Taco Bell.  Runner up is Burger King.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000031||fierospeeder||12-12-2001||02:26 AM||||its amazing that arbys and long john silver are still in business.<P>My house is in a 2 mile radius of all the fast food places.  including arbys and long john silver<P>And my fav is wendys, is a half block away.  To bad i spend 7 bucks there just for myself.||||reg||1
Z||000032||onfire||12-12-2001||03:37 AM||||Nashco, Dicks is pretty good. We also have Taco Time mmmmm crisp beef burrito. Oh, and I forgot Buy's they have a three or a five piece fish and chips. Very good. I can barely finish the three piece. ||||reg||1
Z||000033||Blacktree||12-12-2001||04:26 AM||||<B>Favorite fast food?</B><P>err... a girl on a motorcycle  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000034||Haagster||12-12-2001||05:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>Hasn't anybody heard of Arby's?? Or Long John Silver??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Arby's Beef and Cheddar, curly fries, and a strawberry shake...  Breakfast, lunch and dinner!!!  They have a new thing - the Market Fresh Sandwich(s) that are good too.  <P>Long John's...  NOT!!!  Little fish with LOTS of filler...  Caked in ketsup, maybe...||||reg||6
Z||000035||GTFiero1||12-12-2001||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haagster:<BR><B> Arby's Beef and Cheddar, curly fries, and a strawberry shake...  Breakfast, lunch and dinner!!!  They have a new thing - the Market Fresh Sandwich(s) that are good too.  <P>Long John's...  NOT!!!  Little fish with LOTS of filler...  Caked in ketsup, maybe...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"im so hungry i could even eat at arby's"<BR>"wow she's really hungry"<BR><P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000036||baptistheart||12-13-2001||04:08 AM||||1. Runza<BR>2. K.F.C<BR>3. Arby's<BR>4. Hardee's<BR>5. Wendy's<BR>6. Pizza Hut<BR>7. Burger King<BR>8. Tastee Treat (local i think)<BR>9. Mcdonalds (love breakfast)<BR>10. Godfathers (only place to get pork sausage and sour kraut pizza)<P><BR>and yes my budget for fast food is quite handsom.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000037||GodSend||12-13-2001||09:43 AM||||I cant believe no one has said A&W - The teen burger is awesome.  Seriously, A&W is one of the only places where the burger even remotly resembles the pictures on the menu board .... The lettuce is usually crispy.. and the bacon appears to be real!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">... Yummy (Of course.. Taco Bell is a close second... Arbys is good too! )||||reg||1
